  "notes": "Swedish electropop's \"sad banger\" architect — dancefloor tempo carrying melancholic content, modelled on the 2005-2018 defining window inside the stated 1995-present era. Two research claims drive the numbers. First, the harmony: the documented formula is a number \"with juicy chord changes\", explicitly \"more harmonic motion than the lane's static vamps, with a major-III or VI as the ache\", so `harmonicRhythm` drops the parent's `vamp` weight entirely and the families all move through III or VI. Second, the kit: \"hard four-square kick with a clipped clap on 2&4, offbeat 8th open hats\" gives a kick pinned at exactly four with no syncopation, and \"fills are noise sweeps and gated stutters, not snare rolls\" is why `rolls.freqPerBar` sits at 0.05 and the perc lanes are riser/impact/reverse rather than a hat bed. The bass \"and the kick are deliberately fused into one attack\" is `mirror_kick` at 0.95 with an octave passing tone for the documented per-bar octave jump. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the melody register and the exact roll and perc densities — the research gives \"clipped\", \"conversational and mid-register with a spoken or half-shouted hook\" and \"sound design\", and 112-126 / 64-86 / 0.05 are this author's reading of those directions. ⚠ The tempo band is lane-derived, as the entry says.",
